          "jcr:created": "Tue Sep 16 2025 20:35:54 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<h3>Speaker:</h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Beth Batcher</b>, MSN, APRN, CNS-AG, CEN</span></p>\n<h3>Moderator:&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Alice Benjamin</b>, MSN, ACNS-BC,&nbsp;FNP-C</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Feb 11 2026 18:44:28 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_908007915_copy_": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "text": "<h1><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Webinar: Cognitive offloading for nurses</span></span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Improving focus and reducing mental load</span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">This topic matters to all of us. Why? Because every role in nursing demands critical thinking, constant multi-tasking&nbsp;and fast decisions. And that requires a lot of cognitive bandwidth. In this&nbsp;webinar&nbsp;we’ll&nbsp;talk about the&nbsp;different types&nbsp;of cognitive load and how cognitive overload&nbsp;impacts&nbsp;our performance,&nbsp;safety&nbsp;and overall wellbeing.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The good news is we’re not powerless. Through tools and technology, preparation and processes, we can reduce that cognitive load and make room for better clinical thinking, stronger teamwork, healthier nurses and really improve care. This free on-demand webinar was presented by <a href=\"https://www.nurse.com/\">Nurse.com</a>.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>You will learn:</b></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The types of cognitive load.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">How to recognize&nbsp;effects&nbsp;of cognitive overload.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The impact of cognitive burden&nbsp;in&nbsp;nursing.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Cognitive offloading in clinical practice.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">How to&nbsp;identify&nbsp;tools and technologies that support offloading.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">How offloading improves workflow and outcomes.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">How preparation, processes, and technology reduce cognitive burden and enhance outcomes.&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Feb 11 2026 18:45:26 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
